# Stuff I Did
## Ran

* I've had really bad runners knee for the better part of the month, sadly, and my distance
has really suffered: 47.8km. Pitiful. I think I'm finally on the other side of it though,
and I have a bunch of fun running stuff coming up in September.

## Played
* Most of my playtime this month has gone to [Lies of P](https://store.steampowered.com/app/1627720/Lies_of_P/), which is excellent. I love that a studio took the
  concept of "Steampunk Pinocchio Bloodborne" and turned it into something that's actually
  really solid, with an outstanding parry system to boot. I've finished the base game but am
  holding off on a Rambling Review until I finish the DLC, but it is coming soon :tm:
* I've also been playing [Big Walk](https://store.steampowered.com/app/1478500/Big_Walk/) with a few friends, and it is absolutely amazing.
  I wasn't sure what to expect going in, but it is truly a one of a kind experience. We're
  not quite done yet, but are at the very end, and I'm sad, since hanging out with my
  buddies is a highlight of most weekends.

## Read
### Books
I only finished *one* book this month! To be fair, I've most of the way through two others
(one is my morning metro commute book), but even still.
* That book was *Harry Potter en de Vuurbeker*, the Dutch translation of Goblet of Fire.
  Every time I re-read Harry Potter I find myself unable to stop, and apparently that even
  holds true in other languages.

### Not Books
* With the digital decluttering I was doing this month, I made a concerted effort not to
  read many tech blogs at all (and to even skip out on some of the ones I would usually
  frequent)
* I did, however, take out a newspaper subscription to the Volkskrant, one of the main
  newspapers here in the Netherlands, and have been getting a lot of satisfaction out of
  being able to read through whole articles at a new local cafe every Saturday morning.

## Listened

I forgot to get my `eurydice` output before the month was over and am too lazy to update
the source code at the moment. Sue me. Instead I'll list some good stuff I listened to:
* [Dungeon Vision by Earth Tongue](https://earthtongue.bandcamp.com/album/dungeon-vision) is a psych rock album after my own heart that I've had on repeat the last few days.
* [HUN by The HU](https://thehu.bandcamp.com/album/hun) is hit or miss, but the couple heaters it does have are some of their best (Second Face in particular)
* I found the [Super Mario Galaxy 2 Soundtrack](https://archive.org/details/super-mario-galaxy-2-original-soundtrack) on archive.org and have been having a wonderful time reliving being 10 years old

# Stuff I Only Sorta Did or Didn't Do

* I spent the first couple weeks of the month doing a pretty good amount of digital
  decluttering (as presented in [Digital Minimalism](https://hardcover.app/books/digital-minimalism)), and it honestly felt pretty amazing.
  Sadly, I did not stick to it as much as I should have, for various reasons, but none
  that are really a good excuse.

# Stuff I'm Gonna Do in September
* So I'd like to try again in September! I may reread some of the book first, but I think
  now that I know what to watch out for, and with September being **extremely** busy for
  me, I feel like I stand a much better chance of having some of the habits stick. I plan
  to write a wider post about it as well, once I've had some time to let it sink in (and
  once my life settles down from the current chaos).
* I'm doing *so much shit* in September otherwise, including:
    * Two different running races
    * Two different out-of-the-country long weekend vacations
    * Moving to a different part of Amsterdam!

September is gonna be a bit of a crazy one, and that's also why this recap is so short.
Too many things on the horizon to spend a ton of time looking back.
